@*
    The pace a band's plans are placed at: how many story points a week an imported
    plan with no due date is drawn at, and an in-flight plan is forecast to finish
    at (ADR 0013, ruling 4).

    A slider, because the figure that matters is a place between two others: what
    the lane measured over the last two weeks and what the reader typed in the
    roadmap's heading (PaceSliderRange). A lane that has been dormant measures very
    little, and the reader wants to pull it back towards their own pace without
    opening a field. Letting go of the thumb sets the lane's own pace
    (IPlanningPace.SetOwn, PaceSource.Set), which the band places by from then on;
    the figure beside the slider follows the thumb while it is held.

    "Measured" puts the lane back on the pace it measures: it chooses the last two
    weeks, and is pressed whenever a measured stretch is the one in effect. With
    nothing finished in any stretch there is nothing measured to go back to: it is
    offered only while the slider has set the pace, as "Reset", which returns the band
    to the reader's own pace — and a line then says that pace is placing the band.

    The info mark, at the end of the band's name, says what the lane actually managed
    over the last two, four and eight weeks — the evidence for choosing a pace — and
    which pace is placing it. Every figure is a whole number of points.

    Kept per repository band, because productivity differs from one project to the
    next (ADR 0013, ruling 4 as amended), under the band's name in the chart's
    sidebar, above the band's named lanes, in the rows the band reserves for it
    (RoadmapPlanView.PaceRows). A repository's band carries that repository's pace
    (Repository set), measured over its own finished work. The unfiled band carries
    the default pace (Repository unset), measured over all of it, and its own pace is
    the heading's typed one.

    A change here that alters the pace in use is reported through OnPaceChanged. The
    band redraws on the pace's own change notice instead, every bar still sized by
    its effort, each at its own repository's pace (ADR 0013, ruling 5 as amended).
    Those windows are read, not stored (local ADR 0018), so the choice writes the
    pace and nothing else — once: letting go of the thumb sets the pace and chooses
    it in one save, and the thumb stays where it was let go while that is read back.
*@
@implements IDisposable
@inject IPlanningPace Pace
@inject IRoadmapWorkChanges WorkChanges

<div class="roadmap-pace" data-testid="@TestIdOf(null)">
    @* At the end of the band's name, in the band's top-right corner, where it does
       not take a line of the rows the band reserves (see .roadmap-pace__hint). *@
    <InfoHint CssClass="roadmap-pace__hint"
              AriaLabel="@HintLabel"
              TestId="@TestIdOf("hint")"
              TriggerTestId="@TestIdOf("hint-trigger")"
              TooltipTestId="@TestIdOf("hint-text")">
        <span class="roadmap-pace__hint-line">@Managed</span>
        <span class="roadmap-pace__hint-line">@Placing</span>
    </InfoHint>

    <div class="roadmap-pace__line">
        <Slider CssClass="roadmap-pace__slider"
                Min="_range.Min"
                Max="_range.Max"
                Step="_range.Step"
                Value="_released ?? _paces.InUse"
                ValueInput="OnLive"
                ValueChanged="SetOwn"
                AriaLabel="@SliderLabel"
                ValueText="@($"{Rounded(Shown)} points a week")"
                TestId="@TestIdOf("slider")" />
        <span class="roadmap-pace__value"
              data-testid="@TestIdOf("value")">@Rounded(Shown) pt/wk</span>
    </div>

    <div class="roadmap-pace__line">
        @if (HasMeasured || SetByHand)
        {
            <ToggleButton BaseClass="btn btn--toggle btn--small"
                          CssClass="roadmap-pace__measured"
                          Pressed="Measuring"
                          Title="@MeasuredTitle"
                          OnClick="ChooseMeasured"
                          TestId="@TestIdOf("measured")">
                @(HasMeasured ? "Measured" : "Reset")
            </ToggleButton>
        }

        @* One short line, always the same height, so the band never has to grow for
           it. The whole sentence is its title and what a screen reader hears. *@
        @if (Note is { } note)
        {
            <span class="roadmap-pace__note"
                  role="status"
                  title="@note.Sentence"
                  data-testid="@TestIdOf(note.Kind)">
                <span aria-hidden="true">@note.Short</span>
                <span class="sr-only">@note.Sentence</span>
            </span>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the line under the slider says: a short form to show and the
    /// sentence it stands for.</summary>
    private sealed record PaceNote(string Kind, string Short, string Sentence);

    /// <summary>The repository whose pace this is, by alias; unset for the default
    /// pace — the one a plan filed in no repository is placed at.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Repository { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised after the reader moved the slider or chose the measured pace
    /// and that changed the pace placement uses for this control's scope, so the band
    /// can redraw the bars sized by it. Not raised for a choice that leaves the pace
    /// in use where it was.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnPaceChanged { get; set; }

    private PlanningPacesDto _paces = new(7m, null, null, null, PaceSource.Manual);
    private PaceSliderRange _range = PaceSliderRange.Of(null, 7m, 7m);
    private string? _error;
    private string? _read;
    private bool _initialized;

    /// <summary>The figure the thumb is at while it is held, before it is let go; the
    /// pace in use otherwise.</summary>
    private decimal? _live;

    /// <summary>The figure the thumb was let go at, until the pace it saved has been
    /// read back. Without it the slider is handed the pace in use from before, and
    /// puts the thumb back there for as long as the read takes.</summary>
    private decimal? _released;

    private decimal Shown => _released ?? _live ?? _paces.InUse;

    private string Lane => Repository ?? "all your work";

    private string SliderLabel => Repository is null
        ? "Points a week the default pace places a plan at"
        : $"Points a week plans in {Repository} are placed at";

    private string HintLabel => Repository is null
        ? "About the default pace"
        : $"About the pace in {Repository}";

    private string MeasuredTitle => !HasMeasured
        ? $"Stop using the pace set by hand{Where} and place by your typed pace until something is finished"
        : Repository is null
            ? "Place plans by what you finished over the last two weeks"
            : $"Place {Repository}'s plans by what you finished there over the last two weeks";

    /// <summary>The slider set this scope's pace. With nothing measured, the reset is
    /// the only way back to the typed pace, so it is offered then too.</summary>
    private bool SetByHand => _paces.InEffect == PaceSource.Set;

    private string Where => Repository is null ? string.Empty : $" in {Repository}";

    /// <summary>Whether any stretch measured something — and so whether there is a
    /// measured pace to go back to.</summary>
    private bool HasMeasured => PlanningPacesDto.Stretches.Any(stretch => _paces.Of(stretch) is not null);

    /// <summary>A measured stretch is the one placing this scope.</summary>
    private bool Measuring => _paces.InEffect is PaceSource.LastTwoWeeks or PaceSource.LastFourWeeks or PaceSource.LastEightWeeks;

    /// <summary>What the lane managed, for the info mark.</summary>
    private string Managed =>
        $"Managed{(Repository is null ? " across all your work" : $" in {Repository}")}: "
        + $"last 2 weeks {Stretch(_paces.LastTwoWeeks)} · 4 weeks {Stretch(_paces.LastFourWeeks)} · 8 weeks {Stretch(_paces.LastEightWeeks)}";

    /// <summary>What is placing the lane, for the info mark.</summary>
    private string Placing => $"Placing at {Rounded(_paces.InUse)} pt/wk — " + _paces.InEffect switch
    {
        PaceSource.Set => "set by hand",
        PaceSource.LastTwoWeeks => "measured over 2 weeks",
        PaceSource.LastFourWeeks => "measured over 4 weeks",
        PaceSource.LastEightWeeks => "measured over 8 weeks",
        _ => "your typed pace"
    };

    private static string Stretch(decimal? perWeek) =>
        perWeek is { } pace ? $"{Rounded(pace)} pt/wk" : "nothing finished";

    /// <summary>What the line under the slider says, most pressing first: a choice
    /// that could not be kept, since it is what the reader just did; then, with no
    /// stretch measured and no pace set by hand, that the reader's own pace is placing
    /// this band.</summary>
    private PaceNote? Note
    {
        get
        {
            if (_error is not null) return new PaceNote("refused", "Not saved — see why", _error);

            if (_paces.FellBack)
            {
                var mine = Rounded(_paces.Manual);
                return new PaceNote(
                    "fell-back",
                    $"Using Mine: {mine} pt/wk",
                    $"Nothing estimated was finished{Where} in the last eight weeks, so your own pace is used: {mine} points a week.");
            }

            return null;
        }
    }

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        Pace.Changed += OnChanged;
        WorkChanges.Changed += OnChanged;
        await Read();
        _initialized = true;
    }

    /// <summary>A control handed another repository reads that one's pace.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (!_initialized || string.Equals(_read, Repository, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) return;

        _error = null;
        await Read();
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        Pace.Changed -= OnChanged;
        WorkChanges.Changed -= OnChanged;
    }

    private async Task Read()
    {
        _read = Repository;
        _paces = await Pace.ReadAsync(Repository);
        _live = null;
        _range = PaceSliderRange.Of(_paces.LastTwoWeeks, _paces.Manual, _paces.InUse);
    }

    private void OnLive(decimal value) => _live = value;

    /// <summary>The thumb was let go: the lane's own pace is what it says.</summary>
    private async Task SetOwn(decimal value)
    {
        var before = _paces.InUse;
        _released = value;
        try
        {
            _error = Pace.SetOwn(value, Repository);
            await Read();
        }
        finally
        {
            _released = null;
        }

        if (_paces.InUse != before) await OnPaceChanged.InvokeAsync();
    }

    private async Task ChooseMeasured()
    {
        var before = _paces.InUse;
        _error = Pace.Choose(PaceSource.LastTwoWeeks, Repository);
        await Read();
        if (_paces.InUse != before) await OnPaceChanged.InvokeAsync();
    }

    // Raised from whatever thread saved the pace or wrote a task.
    private void OnChanged() => _ = InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        await Read();
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    /// <summary>Every test id carries the scope at the end — the repository, or
    /// "default" — so each band's control can be told apart.</summary>
    private string TestIdOf(string? part)
    {
        var id = part is null ? "roadmap-pace" : $"roadmap-pace-{part}";
        return $"{id}-{(Repository is null ? "default" : Slug(Repository))}";
    }

    private static string Slug(string value) =>
        new([.. value.Select(character => char.IsLetterOrDigit(character) ? char.ToLowerInvariant(character) : '-')]);

    /// <summary>A pace as a whole number of points, the only figure the slider sets.
    /// Placement still divides by the figure it was measured to.</summary>
    private static string Rounded(decimal pace) =>
        Math.Round(pace, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero).ToString("0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
}
